  "vibe": "Mahogany #3a2618 and #1c1410 ink lit by brass #c9a24b, with oxblood #7a2e2e saved for the things that count down. Cinzel's inscriptional capitals stamp in from 1.7× scale with a 6° twist; Radio Canada does the plain speaking. The world is a Victorian study that is also a puzzle: a wall clock whose oxblood second hand sweeps in real time above a slow brass hour hand, two counter-rotating cog wheels, a keyhole monument throwing a faint brass light beam, and a brass padlock at the front whose shackle actually swings open partway through every single beat. This is the most restless camera here — the set steps by seven, rotation 0.8, a spin move included, and only a 20% settle before the title lands.",
